{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127722,"nonce":"t3fS0OLoGKzV1It/UVWl9VYx2fo=","title":"Console session creation: SDK vs Channel mode selector","message":"The NewSessionDialog needs a third transport option for Claude sessions: \"Channel\" alongside \"SDK\" and \"PTY\". Channel mode launches Claude CLI with --channels server:mandible in a PTY, giving terminal visibility plus channel integration.\n\n## Current state\nNewSessionDialog offers:\n- Kind: Chat agent / Operator\n- Backend: Claude Code / Codex / Gemini\n- Transport (Claude only): SDK / PTY\n\n## Proposed\nAdd \"Channel\" as a transport option for Claude:\n- SDK: Mandible spawns Claude via Agent SDK. Requires API key. Full control.\n- Channel: Mandible launches claude --channels server:mandible in a PTY. User OAuth. Terminal + channel tools.\n- PTY (deprecated): Raw terminal only. No structured events.\n\n## UI changes\n- OptionCard for Channel mode with description explaining OAuth/zero-config benefits\n- Preset selector behavior differs: SDK shows full preset selector, Channel shows preset-at-creation-only notice\n- Channel mode should be the DEFAULT for new users (no API key needed)\n- Badge or indicator showing which mode a running session uses\n\n## Backend changes\n- backend_type \"channel\" in ConsoleSessionInput and ConsoleSession\n- Session creation builds the launch command: claude --channels server:mandible [--system-prompt \"...\"] [--append-system-prompt \"...\"]\n- Presets applied via --system-prompt/--append-system-prompt CLI flags at launch\n\n## Dependencies\n- Channel terminal view (ca3d052)\n- Channel server (73e0adf) — done","files":null}]}